Save93 / Whiterun exterior / DynDOLOD FormList.GetAt return lock / 2026-11-09

Measurement
- Use the last completing DynDOLOD ObjectEnabler stack per exterior return. In some trials a different script is last overall. Each identified target had eight completed GetAt calls. The measured return span is from completed native marshalling (N) to VM frame completion (O).
- Pair the failed return acquire and later successful acquire (L/A) on the same stack, depth and object token. Reconstruct the token timeline from successful acquisition (G), full release (X), release with flag (Z) and flag setting (B). Intersect the observed spans with N->O. A free span requires a full release followed by an acquisition without a contradictory intervening failure. Conflicting or incomplete transitions remain unknown.
- 'free_to_other' ends with another stack acquiring the token. 'free_to_target' ends with the selected waiting stack acquiring it. These buckets describe the observed scheduling and do not prove that the target was first in the scheduler's eligible queue.
- For each time span when another DynDOLOD stack held the token, intersect its actual depth-1 Q->P native call waits. Percentages are computed per trial and summarized by median. This overlap identifies what the lock holder was waiting for.
- Rows are per-trial sums. Their medians can differ from the sum of the individual median buckets.
- Prior raw inputs: the two off trials from cell-42-continuation-budget-ab (normal render configuration), and eight off trials from cell-42-continuation-replication-no-fg and its reverse launch. Same Save93, SSE Display Tweaks 42 FPS cap and dynamic Papyrus budget. The second group had SkyrimUpscaler frame generation disabled in the disposable profile.
- New observation mode getat-return-observe logs the original suspended-stack retry pass boundary, float budget, and both queue heads under the engine's queue lock. It uses the existing stock VM scheduling. Neither the native drain nor the suspended queue order is edited. The capture checks whether a >5 ms final free interval overlapped an already-running pass that hit its budget, left the target first and did not try it. This gate excludes any case requiring a new pass, queue swap, or overtaking.
- Build SHA256 5D2E058BE8957D159DD80A6960775F0997A164DE99EE1023257C3D501790E836. Build and budget policy tests passed. Synthetic partitions exercised held/free classification, contradictory transitions, an ordered budget candidate and exclusions.
- First new observation launch stopped during the first exterior return. Windows reported c0000005 at SkyrimSE.exe+CC90CF (Address Library AE ID 68233 +0xF, BSReadWriteLock::LockForRead). No finished window was collected and attribution is undetermined.

