Decision and cleanup
- The four new stock windows completed all 128 probes. All 1499 observed stock retry starts paired with an end and queue snapshot. Each tail's final free time summed to 0.014–0.206 ms. None had a final free gap over 5 ms. Among 81 longer gaps ending in another stack's acquisition, no stock retry pass ended before the other acquisition. The already-running-pass budget gate produced zero candidates.
- The long free gaps are observed latency. Letting the selected tail take the token during a gap which ended in a different owner would change the recorded acquisition sequence. Rescheduling or adding another pass is outside the ordering constraint for this comparison.
- The principal remaining engine investigation is the lock holder's own stock GetWorldSpace Q->P. Its overlap represented 87.967% of the other-DynDOLOD hold time by median in the previous ten trials, and 85.725% in the fresh four trials. This identifies a queue wait rather than native callback cost. It does not yet identify whether the native message was available during an earlier stock drain.
- Prior comparable stock baseline (eight frame-generation-off trials): arrival-to-drain 2236.275 ms, response p95 39.913 ms, steady render p99 24.268 ms. Fresh stock observation has the values printed above. Both are stock baselines. No acceleration A/B was run because an eligible order-preserving opportunity was not observed.
- The re-run completed. PresentMon exited with code 0. The original MO2 selection was restored and the disposable fixture archived. Save93 hashes remain ESS 87C181889BB60A565C327FF0AA0B1B6F46D568AC0EB29C022925A3912742277D and SKSE 5EE67E98B488FAE5BD5C1E5A9A87DA9D92522D480255F2F1BA84E6FB80F1B0AA. Original SkyrimUpscaler.ini SHA256 3CF1A335E01731D2A40A884D7A2335AF55009B29B06DB739EB397566F299677E.
